            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Chenopodium ficifolium, the fig-leaved goosefoot or figleaf goosefoot, is a plant species in the family Amaranthaceae originally native to the Irano-Turanian floristic region. It is an archaeophyte weed in Europe and can now be found in temperate crop-growing regions in most of the world."
